<title>USA: USDA's Glickman won't boost sugar import quota.</title>
<headline>USDA's Glickman won't boost sugar import quota.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Agriculture Secretary Dan Glickman said Wednesday he would not increase the U.S. sugar import quota, despite concerns among food processors.</p>
<p>&quot;I don't think so,&quot; Glickman said when asked if he would use his authority to increase the quota. &quot;We're going to let the program work for a while.&quot;</p>
<p>USDA adopted a formula to determine when to adjust the quota this fiscal year. The formula was used for the first time last week and forecast a sugar supply too large to allow a 200,000 tonne increase in the quota.</p>
</text>
